[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Restart the panel ("xfce4-panel -r", or log out and in again) and add the
panel item "Bluetooth (FreeBSD)".  bsdbt(1) does the same from the command
line.

The adapter needs its firmware loaded and the Bluetooth stack started;
devd does both when the firmware package is installed (for example
rtlbt-firmware or iwmbt-firmware).

Pairing a device enables hcsecd (and bthidd for keyboards and mice) in
/etc/rc.conf and starts them.

The plugin runs %%PREFIX%%/libexec/bsdbt-helper through pkexec.  If
pkexec fails with a "Last login" message, give pkexec's PAM service a
session stack without pam_lastlog in %%PREFIX%%/etc/pam.d/polkit-1
(replace "session include system" with "session required pam_permit.so").
EOM
}
{ type: remove
  message: <<EOM
The devices set up stay in /etc/bluetooth/hcsecd.conf and bthidd.conf
(marked "# managed by bsdbt"), and hcsecd_enable/bthidd_enable stay in
/etc/rc.conf.
EOM
}
]
